        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "fg-notes",
          "name": "Design notes",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 16,
          "fill": "$surface-light",
          "cornerRadius": 6,
          "stroke": { "align": "inside", "thickness": 1, "fill": "$border-light" },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fg-notes-hdr",
              "fill": "$mars-night",
              "content": "Design notes for implementation",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fg-notes-body",
              "fill": "$muted-light",
              "content": "1. NODE SHAPES: Task nodes use a solid-border rectangle. Idea nodes use a dashed-border rectangle (same geometry, different stroke). This matches ia-decision.md §vocabulary: distinguished by stroke style, not by color, so the semantic palette applies uniformly to both.\n\n2. EDGE ROUTING: Long lineage edges (e.g. IDEA → current task spanning all columns) route along the top gutter (y≈22) to avoid crossing interior nodes. Implementation may substitute an orthogonal router or curved spline — the constraint is legibility of the label, not the exact path.\n\n3. STATUS COLOR MAPPING (semantic palette, v1): succeeded → $mars-ice (teal); in-flight → $mars-amber; needs-attention → $mars-rust; not-started → $mars-basalt. These map one-to-one to semantic intent, not to granular task-status enum values. A single in-flight task and a recovering task both render as amber.\n\n4. RECOVERY-FAILED BADGE: Positioned at the top-right corner of the fix-task node, overlapping the node border. The badge text is the inbox item kind (recovery-failed | no-recipe). Clicking the badge is the sole write affordance — it navigates to /mars:inbox, it does not act in place.\n\n5. DEPTH DEGENERACY: A task with no idea ancestor and no blockers renders as a single node in column 0 (it IS the root). The canvas degenerates to a single node; this is expected and self-explanatory per ia-decision.md §decision.\n\n6. TOKENS USED: $mars-ice is referenced as the 'succeeded' status color; it exists in design/ui.pen. All other tokens ($mars-amber, $mars-rust, $mars-basalt, $mars-night, $surface-light, $bg-light, $border-light, $muted-light) are already present in the design system.",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }

      ]
    }
  ]
